  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, AI, and cloud storage optimization. Key developments include: an initial introduction and kick-off in June/July 2023 with a $500,000 budget for Phase One led by Sarah Tan (later Marcus Cole is mentioned as leader in another update); a call for R&D ideas by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization; strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research; team expansion with experts in machine learning and cloud computing; a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two; completion of the testing phase and a celebration on October 10th; a staff meeting on November 20th to share detailed reports; and a request for stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
